Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by the failure of the `TestAuthFilterAuthOozieClient` test case after changes made in OOZIE-1917, which likely altered the authentication mechanism or configuration handling, leading to incorrect assumptions about system properties and their effects on the test environment. The test was not properly configured to handle the new authentication settings, resulting in failures when running the tests.

